        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Anubis\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/anubis/48/4949_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Anubis:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Each Villain has a unique mechanic to determine status die.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ah ha! I missed that in the book. “…their status does not come from their Health, but from a story or mechanical element - something that the villain cares about…”</p>\n<p>Thank you for pointing that out! In the example on page 18 of the Gameplay Guide, Proletariat cares about how many clones he has going on.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wish I had a way to upvote this post or something, just for the word “midimum”. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
